<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<assembly manifestVersion="1.0" xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v1">
  <assemblyIdentity version="1.0.0.0" name="KitveiHakodeshService.app"/>
  <trustInfo xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v2">
    <security>
      <requestedPrivileges xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v3">
        <!--
          asInvoker — deliberately NOT requireAdministrator. This is the right setting for
          BOTH modes this exe runs in, which is why it must not change:
            - dev: spawned from a normal terminal, inherits its token, stays rebuildable.
            - production: registered as a LocalSystem Windows service, which receives its
              privileges from the SCM. A service does not need — and does not use — a
              requireAdministrator manifest to run elevated.

          What admin rights buy: NTFS USN journal access (FSCTL_READ_USN_JOURNAL,
          FSCTL_ENUM_USN_DATA), which gives PathIndex a fast MFT build AND the live
          file-system watcher.

          Do NOT read the fallback below as "elevation is optional for the product". The
          BUILD degrades gracefully; the WATCHER does not degrade, it disappears:
            - PathIndex.Build falls back to FallbackCrawler (directory walk), which
              indexes the same extensions and skips the same folders, so the index is
              equivalent — just slower to build the first time.
            - PathIndex.StartLiveUpdates pre-flights UsnJournal.CanOpenVolume and returns
              immediately when the volume handle is refused. There is no FileSystemWatcher
              anywhere in DocumentLocator, so an unelevated index is FROZEN at build time —
              it never sees files the user adds, deletes, or renames. Acceptable in dev,
              not in production. That is precisely why production registers this as a
              LocalSystem service.

          requireAdministrator was tried and REVERTED: a hard elevation request makes
          CreateProcess fail outright with ERROR_ELEVATION_REQUIRED (-4094) from any
          non-elevated parent. That broke `npm run dev` from a normal terminal — vite
          spawns this exe, the spawn failed, so /khs-endpoint 503'd forever and the whole
          dev data path was dead unless the terminal itself was restarted elevated.
          asInvoker means we inherit the parent's token: elevated parent → USN fast path
          and live updates; normal parent → fallback crawl. Either way we always START.
        -->
        <requestedExecutionLevel level="asInvoker" uiAccess="false"/>
      </requestedPrivileges>
    </security>
  </trustInfo>
  <compatibility xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:compatibility.v1">
    <application>
      <!-- Windows 10 / 11 -->
      <supportedOS Id="{8e0f7a12-bfb3-4fe8-b9a5-48fd50a15a9a}"/>
    </application>
  </compatibility>
</assembly>
